00:39:12.949 --> 00:39:15.952
By the way, there's 40,000 of
these membranes in this plant.

00:39:15.952 --> 00:39:19.723
Each one is 2 meters long
and 40 square meters of area.

00:39:19.723 --> 00:39:24.194
So-- so these are so delicate
that you can't really

00:39:24.194 --> 00:39:25.729
clean them well.

00:39:25.729 --> 00:39:28.598
And that's part of what the
cost of a plant involves.

00:39:28.598 --> 00:39:30.667
That's part of what the
cost of a plant involves.

00:39:30.667 --> 00:39:32.669
Now, this would be like
a plant, right, you

00:39:32.669 --> 00:39:36.039
have sea water coming in
and, you know-- and then

00:39:36.039 --> 00:39:37.874
you've got your membrane
module that's taking

00:39:37.874 --> 00:39:39.676
the salt out of the water.

00:39:39.676 --> 00:39:40.844
And then the product water.

00:39:40.844 --> 00:39:44.514
But because this
filter is so delicate--

00:39:44.514 --> 00:39:45.682
there's the picture--

00:39:45.682 --> 00:39:47.150
because that filter
is so delicate,

00:39:47.150 --> 00:39:49.686
you actually have to add a
whole lot more to the plant.

00:39:49.686 --> 00:39:52.956
So much of a desal plant
is built around essentially

00:39:52.956 --> 00:39:55.625
protecting this membrane.

00:39:55.625 --> 00:39:56.693
So that's cost.

00:39:56.693 --> 00:39:58.395
That's cost.

00:39:58.395 --> 00:39:58.895
Right.

00:39:58.895 --> 00:40:01.498
A better membrane
could change this.

00:40:01.498 --> 00:40:03.800
But like I said, the
membrane-- oh, there it is.

00:40:03.800 --> 00:40:07.437
You can't Snapchat on that.

00:40:07.437 --> 00:40:08.071
