me the equivalent two sigma

00:45:15.111 --> 00:45:15.812
bonds.

00:45:15.812 --> 00:45:21.751
Be starts with these
as electrons filled.

00:45:21.751 --> 00:45:24.020
Right.

00:45:24.020 --> 00:45:28.658
But if Be had something
more like this,

00:45:28.658 --> 00:45:33.229
if it had an sp electron
in each of those orbitals,

00:45:33.229 --> 00:45:39.502
well, now, when I see the two h
orbitals, the two 1 SH orbitals

00:45:39.502 --> 00:45:42.772
coming at me, I can form
those equivalent bonds.

00:45:42.772 --> 00:45:45.241
So BeH2 will also
hybridize [INAUDIBLE]

00:45:45.241 --> 00:45:47.510
to make that molecule.

00:45:47.510 --> 00:45:49.145
And all sorts of other things.

00:45:49.145 --> 00:45:51.347
The deal orbitals can
get in on the action.

00:45:51.347 --> 00:45:51.881
All right.

00:45:51.881 --> 00:45:53.983
So here's SF6, which
