00:45:59.989 --> 00:46:02.859
But, now, you know that
the way this actually

00:46:02.859 --> 00:46:05.428
works because these
are equivalent bonds.

00:46:05.428 --> 00:46:09.365
So the only way this can work
is if I form hybrid orbitals.

00:46:09.365 --> 00:46:09.899
Right.

00:46:09.899 --> 00:46:10.366
Right.

00:46:10.366 --> 00:46:12.769
But they didn't have
to be equivalent bonds

00:46:12.769 --> 00:46:15.271
until we learned about VSEPR.

00:46:15.271 --> 00:46:19.242
And it said, no, I want
to maximize my separation

00:46:19.242 --> 00:46:20.443
to minimize repulsions.

00:46:20.443 --> 00:46:24.080
And so then we know that if
they're equivalent bonds,

00:46:24.080 --> 00:46:26.816
the energy of the
system will be lower.

00:46:26.816 --> 00:46:27.917
Right.

00:46:27.917 --> 00:46:29.919
And so that-- that's--

00:46:29.919 --> 00:46:32.655
you know, that's going to
have to take some d orbitals

00:46:32.655 --> 00:46:35.158
and create these
hybrid orbitals.

00:46:35.158 --> 00:46:36.159
Look, they're beautiful.

00:46:36.159 --> 00:46:39.929
Because, now, this thing from
the sulfur, this thing can say,

00:46:39.929 --> 00:46:43.266
hey, I can take six of you,
and I can be equivalent bonding

00:46:43.266 --> 00:46:44.200
to all of you.

00:46:44.200 --> 00:46:46.402
That's what hybridization is.

00:46:46.402 --> 00:46:47.103
OK.

